Hey [~accountid:712020:8c797c70-7a57-496e-aa3f-5d91df806eb2] , here replies from the Customer we were waiting for:

# Can you please clarify what information will be shared under the Act No.340/2015 Coll. on the register of contracts? We would like to know whether the entire agreement will be shared or only specific basic data, and in case only limited data will be shared we would like to know which data will be shared. {color:#bf2600}The Act on the Register of Contracts defines 4 basic data that must remain visible in the contract, namely a) identification of the contracting parties, b) definition of the subject of the contract, c) price, and if the contract does not include it, the value of the subject of the contract, if it can be determined, and d) date of conclusion of the contract. If you wish to erase something in the contract, can we please color code it in some way so that we can look at it and possibly agree on what to do next? However, the 4 above-mentioned data must remain legible.{color}
# Could you please provide clarification regarding why the agreement shall be effective only after the publication of the data regarding it under the Act No.340/2015 Coll.? Is there something that prevents you from concluding a valid agreement prior to publication on the register of contracts? {color:#bf2600}There must have been a communication error here. Of course, the contract comes into force on the date of signature of all contracting parties. However, the contract will only become effective on the day it is published in the register of contracts. ČEB is, according to Act 340/2015 Coll. public enterprise (§2, para. 1. letter m)) and as such has the obligation to publish the contracts it concludes in the register of contracts with various exceptions. Unfortunately, there is no non-disclosure exception for this type of contract. The reason why it becomes effective only after publication is stated in §6, paragraph 1 of the Act - "A contract subject to the obligation to publish through the contract register becomes effective on the date of publication first"{color}

Best

Miroslava

