Hey [~accountid:621d26539c3cce00694a1b14] jumping in here

{quote}We know that drivers are removed the access to cash after a certain amount of debt, but we don't know how much is this amount?{quote}

Yes, this is true. All drivers who are using driver-based invoicing will be cash-blocked if they start to accumulate large amounts of debt. This means cash rides will become unavailable but the driver can still accept in-app & card rides. To track the city-level cash-blocking thresholds you can use this Looker report - [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/21670?toggle=fil&qid=4Ee8J50OLer3u1OUnaRsL3|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/looks/21670?toggle=fil&qid=4Ee8J50OLer3u1OUnaRsL3]

{quote}Is there any block after a certain amount or time with the debt?{quote}

Cash-blocking is automatically enabled for all drivers under driver-based invoicing (not fleet drivers). As per the report above it seems like the threshold is 30 eur. The drivers will get automatic notifications once they get cash-blocked & are required to either make a manual payment to clear their debt or a few in-app rides from which we can cover their debt automatically. 

{quote}Any other set up as part of the process?{quote}

As Belgium is in-app heavy market we don’t have much issues with driver debt in BE. You can keep track of driver debt using this Looker dashboard [https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/16992?Country+Name=Belgium&City+Name=&Fleet+ID=&Driver+ID=&Due+Date+Date=12+month+ago+for+12+month|https://bolt.cloud.looker.com/dashboards/16992?Country+Name=Belgium&City+Name=&Fleet+ID=&Driver+ID=&Due+Date+Date=12+month+ago+for+12+month] and check the drivers who might have a debt issue & potentially reach out to push them to make a payment. But in general there’s no need for thorough investigation as the debt impact is very small in Belgium

