The agreement was that Visjonel would prepare the warehouse for scooter operations, essentially ensuring that we had the necessary infrastructure available for charging batteries. The agreement was that we should be able to charge 750 batteries per cycle, but once the work was completed, we could only charge 350 batteries per cycle, which had a significant impact on our daily operations.

This subpar delivery led us to seek an evaluation from two different companies to check the work performed by Visjonel. As described by Jose in the attached email, the job was unsatisfactory:

# Work performed is under dimensioned;
# The work was not planned according to Bolt's needs (and all the information was provided by Bolt to Visjonel long before the job was performed);
# the main current breaker at 63 A and we have the capacity to 96 A;
# We are not maximizing 18 fuses of 16 A each;
# The main breaker is overloaded; 6. Earth is faulty, some current is escaping as shown by the white markers in the fuse boxes;
# The main wires are undersized (10mm cable instead of 17mm);
# Cable covers are not set, and there is a risk of electric shock;
# New overload protection was not marked; 
# The setup done is not set according to the local regulations; the cables and plugs, for example, are not securely fastened;
# Lack of declaration of conformity, final control, and risk assessment.
# We can never charge more than 350 per cycle as opposed to the 700 agreed initially

In the end, we ended up hiring another company to complete the job. As mentioned, I do not have more information available as all communication took place between Jose and Visjonel. I can check with IT to see if they can access emails sent between Jose and Visjonel.


