Hello, reason it failed it due to high write ratio on PRELIVE + online DDL, causing duplicate key:


{quote}When running an online DDL operation, the thread that runs the {{ALTER TABLE}} statement applies an online log of DML operations that were run concurrently on the same table from other connection threads. When the DML operations are applied, it is possible to encounter a duplicate key entry error ({{ERROR 1062 (23000): Duplicate entry}}), even if the duplicate entry is only temporary and would be reverted by a later entry in the online log. This is similar to the idea of a foreign key constraint check in {{InnoDB}} in which constraints must hold during a transaction.{quote}

To get around this on PRELIVE, I had to lock the table and run the ALTER manually.

{noformat}mysql> ALTER TABLE `taxify_invoicing2`.`client` ADD COLUMN `payout_client_account_version` bigint unsigned NOT NULL DEFAULT '0' AFTER `vat_code`;
ERROR 1062 (23000): Duplicate entry '4252280' for key 'unique'


mysql> LOCK TABLES `taxify_invoicing2`.`client` WRITE;
Query OK, 0 rows affected (2.48 sec)

mysql> ALTER TABLE `taxify_invoicing2`.`client` ADD COLUMN `payout_client_account_version` bigint unsigned NOT NULL DEFAULT '0' AFTER `vat_code`;
Query OK, 0 rows affected (3 min 58.47 sec)
Records: 0  Duplicates: 0  Warnings: 0

mysql> UNLOCK TABLES;
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.00 sec){noformat}

This should not happen on LIVE as it uses gh-ost method to do the ALTER TABLE, not online DDL.

